body:
Agentic authoring (deck form): both `kalide init` and `kalide init <path>` write a project-root `AGENTS.md` — a single Markdown file giving coding agents a complete, accurate reference to the current kalide deck and template format so they can author decks without guessing. Both deck forms write the SAME guide: the format is identical whether the library is the local `templates/` (no-arg form) or the configured external `templates:` path (`kalide init <path>`); only where the library lives and that the external form writes an empty `slides/` with no starter slide differ, and the guide states both. `AGENTS.md` is the only artifact shipped (no `.opencode/agents/` role files, no machine-readable schema file), written verbatim from a static, authored file embedded in internal/scaffold alongside the hello seed. It is unbranded (no EY branding and no reference to files under `brand/`), text-only, offline, and NOT a template asset: it sits at the deck root, is not part of the deck or library layout, and is never read by the load/validate/render/serve/list code paths, so it does not affect `kalide start` (global.constraint.no-embedded-template-assets, requirements.constraint.brand-not-embedded).

The guide MUST be a complete, accurate reference for the format as implemented, covering (each item traceable to the named requirement):
- the deck layout: `kalide.yaml`, `slides/`, `assets/`, and the resolved library (local `templates/` or the configured `templates:` path; external-template-library);
- `kalide.yaml` keys: `title` (required), `author`, `date` (YYYY-MM-DD), `theme` (default `default`), `navigation` (default|linear|grid), `properties`, `templates` (deck-config, navigation-mode, deck-properties);
- slide files: YAML frontmatter at the very top of the file (line 1) with `template:` naming a slide template, body after the closing `---`; slide naming and ordering; vertical slides; unique slide labels; sections and their frontmatter; speaker notes (slide-template-required, slide-file-ordering, vertical-slides, unique-slide-labels, slide-sections, section-frontmatter, speaker-notes);
- the `templates/` library layout: `library.yaml`, `slides/<name>/`, `sections/<name>/`, `themes/<name>/`, `media/`, and the unknown-entry rule (templates-dir-layout);
- `template.yaml` schema: `description`, `fields` (name, type, required, default, limits, variants, formats/default format, description), `sections` (name, accepted templates, min/max) and the `body` rule; no `usage:` key; `example.md` as the example (template-manifest, field-types, body-rules, template-composition, template-variants, number-date-formats);
- `layout.html.tmpl`: standard Go html/template only; the v1 helper set is exactly `media "path"` (path relative to `media/`, no `..`, no absolute paths); a body, `text` fields and rendered sections arrive as safe HTML while other fields are typed values; the reserved `.deck`/`.slide` context (`.deck.title`, `.deck.author`, `.deck.date`, `.deck.properties`, `.slide.number` string, `.slide.total` integer) (template-language, template-context, deck-data-in-templates);
- themes: token-only stylesheets, no built-in theme, `default` implicit, available themes are the resolved library's `themes/` directories (theme-selection, global.constraint.theme-tokens-only, global.constraint.no-per-slide-styling); media reference rules (template-media);
- validation and errors: fail-fast, exactly one error naming file, line, path, what is wrong and how to fix it, the same text in terminal and browser (error-reporting, whole-deck-validation, closest-match-suggestions);
- the CLI: `init`, `init-library`, `start`, `templates`, `templates <name>`, `version` (cli-commands), with `kalide start` as the validation gate.
The guide MUST instruct agents to discover a project's real templates with `kalide templates` / `kalide templates <name>` and to validate with `kalide start` rather than guessing template names, field names or themes. A build/test-time self-test guards the guide against drift from the implemented format (agent-guide-drift-check).

AC:
- immediately after `kalide init`, `AGENTS.md` exists at the project root and `kalide start` still validates and serves the starter deck cleanly (the file is inert to the loader);
- immediately after `kalide init ../lib` against a resolvable library, `AGENTS.md` exists at the deck root and `kalide start` validates and serves from `../lib`;
- the guide contains no EY branding and no reference to files under `brand/`, and no more than the single Markdown file is written;
- the example snippets in the guide, copied into a fresh project, validate via `kalide start` without error.
